--TEST--
`$x is property<T>`, `is propertyPath<T>` and `is string<K>` are `E0867`, alone or in a union, because each is a plain string at run time, and the help names the other type of the union and `as ?` (`rule:types/type-test`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Filter {}

class Customer {
    public string $name = "Ada";

    public static function key(property<Customer>|Filter $x): bool {
        return $x is property<Customer>;
    }

    public static function path(propertyPath<Customer>|Filter $x): bool {
        return $x is propertyPath<Customer>|null;
    }

    public static function holes(string<property<Customer>>|Filter $x): bool {
        return $x is string<property<Customer>>;
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0867]: `is` cannot test for `property<Customer>`
%A
8 |         return $x is property<Customer>;
%A
  = help: a `property<Customer>` is a string while the program runs. Test for the other type of the union instead, such as `$x is SomeClass`, or check a string with `$s as ?property<Customer>`, which gives `null` when the string is wrong
%A
error[E0867]: `is` cannot test for `propertyPath<Customer>`
%A
12 |         return $x is propertyPath<Customer>|null;
%A
error[E0867]: `is` cannot test for `string<property<Customer>>`
%A
16 |         return $x is string<property<Customer>>;
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
